{"id":"mahabharata-3-214","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":214,"title":"चतुर्दशाधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 214 · The birth of Skanda","summary":{"en":"Svaha takes the forms of six of the sages' wives, though not of the faithful Arundhati, and unites with Agni, casting his seed each time into a golden pool on the White Mountain. From it is born Skanda with six heads, who in his first days shakes the mountains and the worlds bow to him.","kn":"ಸ್ವಾಹಾ ಪತಿವ್ರತೆ ಅರುಂಧತಿಯನ್ನು ಬಿಟ್ಟು ಆರು ಋಷಿಪತ್ನಿಯರ ರೂಪ ಧರಿಸಿ ಅಗ್ನಿಯೊಂದಿಗೆ ಕೂಡಿ, ಪ್ರತಿಬಾರಿ ಶ್ವೇತಪರ್ವತದ ಸುವರ್ಣ ಕುಂಡದಲ್ಲಿ ಅವನ ವೀರ್ಯವನ್ನು ಹಾಕುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಅದರಿಂದ ಆರು ತಲೆಗಳ ಸ್ಕಂದನು ಹುಟ್ಟಿ ಮೊದಲ ದಿನಗಳಲ್ಲೇ ಪರ್ವತಗಳನ್ನು ನಡುಗಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಲೋಕಗಳು ಅವನಿಗೆ ನಮಿಸುತ್ತವೆ.","hi":"स्वाहा पतिव्रता अरुन्धती को छोड़ छह ऋषिपत्नियों के रूप धरकर अग्नि से मिलती हैं और हर बार उनका वीर्य श्वेत पर्वत के एक स्वर्ण-कुण्ड में डालती हैं। उससे छह मुखों वाले स्कन्द जन्म लेते हैं, जो पहले ही दिनों में पर्वतों को हिला देते हैं और लोक उन्हें प्रणाम करते हैं।","te":"స్వాహా పతివ్రత అరుంధతిని వదిలి ఆరుగురు ఋషిపత్నుల రూపాలు ధరించి అగ్నితో కలిసి, ప్రతిసారి శ్వేతపర్వతంపై బంగారు కుండంలో అతని వీర్యాన్ని ఉంచుతుంది. దాని నుండి ఆరు ముఖాల స్కందుడు జన్మించి మొదటి రోజుల్లోనే పర్వతాలను కదిలిస్తాడు, లోకాలు అతనికి నమస్కరిస్తాయి.","ta":"ஸ்வாஹா கற்புடைய அருந்ததியைத் தவிர ஆறு முனிவர் மனைவியரின் உருவங்களை ஏற்று அக்னியுடன் கூடி, ஒவ்வொரு முறையும் வெள்ளி மலையிலுள்ள பொற்குளத்தில் அவன் வித்தை இடுகிறாள். அதிலிருந்து ஆறு தலைகள் கொண்ட ஸ்கந்தன் பிறந்து முதல் நாட்களிலேயே மலைகளை நடுங்கச் செய்ய, உலகங்கள் அவனை வணங்குகின்றன.","ml":"വിശ്വസ്തയായ അരുന്ധതി ഒഴികെ ആറു മുനിപത്നിമാരുടെ രൂപം സ്വാഹ സ്വീകരിച്ച് അഗ്നിയോടൊപ്പം ചേരുന്നു; ഓരോ തവണയും ശ്വേതപർവതത്തിലെ സ്വർണ്ണക്കുളത്തിലേക്ക് അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ ബീജം പകരുന്നു. അതിൽനിന്ന് ആറു തലകളുള്ള സ്കന്ദൻ ജനിക്കുന്നു; ജനിച്ച് ആദ്യ ദിവസങ്ങളിൽത്തന്നെ അദ്ദേഹം പർവതങ്ങളെ ഇളക്കുന്നു, ലോകങ്ങൾ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന് മുന്നിൽ വണങ്ങുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.214; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"मार्कण्डेयसमास्यापर्व","titleEn":"Markandeyasamasya Parva (Session with Markandeya)","verses":[{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"शिवा भार्या त्वङ्गिरसः शीलरूपगुणान्विता ।\nतस्याः सा प्रथमं रूपं कृत्वा देवी जनाधिप ।\nजगाम पावकाभ्याशं तं चोवाच वराङ्गना ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Shiva was the wife of Angiras, endowed with good character, beauty and virtue. King, the goddess Svaha first took her form and went to Agni, and the lovely woman said to him...\""}},{"n":2,"text":"मामग्ने कामसंतप्तां त्वं कामयितुमर्हसि ।\nकरिष्यसि न चेदेवं मृतां मामुपधारय ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Agni, I am burning with desire; you ought to make love to me. If you do not, know that I will die.'\""}},{"n":3,"text":"अहमङ्गिरसो भार्या शिवा नाम हुताशन ।\nसखीभिः सहिता प्राप्ता मन्त्रयित्वा विनिश्चयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'I am Shiva, Angiras's wife, offering-bearer. I have come with my friends after deciding it together.'\""}},{"text":"अग्निरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Agni said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"कथं मां त्वं विजानीषे कामार्तमितराः कथम् ।\nयास्त्वया कीर्तिताः सर्वाः सप्तर्षीणां प्रियाः स्त्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'How do you know that I am tormented by desire? And how do the others know, those wives of the seven sages that you have named?'\""}},{"text":"शिवोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shiva said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"अस्माकं त्वं प्रियो नित्यं बिभीमस्तु वयं तव ।\nत्वच्चित्तमिङ्गितैर्ज्ञात्वा प्रेषितास्मि तवान्तिकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'You have always been dear to us, though we fear you. Knowing your mind from your signs, I was sent to you.'\""}},{"n":6,"text":"मैथुनायेह संप्राप्ता कामं प्राप्तं द्रुतं चर ।\nमातरो मां प्रतीक्षन्ते गमिष्यामि हुताशन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'I have come here for union; fulfill your desire quickly. The other women are waiting for me, and I must go, Agni.'\""}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"ततोऽग्निरुपयेमे तां शिवां प्रीतिमुदायुतः ।\nप्रीत्या देवी च संयुक्ता शुक्रं जग्राह पाणिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then Agni, full of joy, took Shiva as his own. Joined with him in love, the goddess received his seed in her hand.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"अचिन्तयन्ममेदं ये रूपं द्रक्ष्यन्ति कानने ।\nते ब्राह्मणीनामनृतं दोषं वक्ष्यन्ति पावके ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"She thought: 'Whoever sees this form of mine in the forest will falsely blame the brahmin women for this fault with Agni.'\""}},{"n":9,"text":"तस्मादेतद्रक्ष्यमाणा गरुडी संभवाम्यहम् ।\nवनान्निर्गमनं चैव सुखं मम भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'So to protect this I will become a female garuda, and leaving the forest will also be easy for me.'\""}},{"n":10,"text":"सुपर्णी सा तदा भूत्वा निर्जगाम महावनात् ।\nअपश्यत्पर्वतं श्वेतं शरस्तम्बैः सुसंवृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Becoming a bird, she then left the great forest. She saw a white mountain, thickly covered with clumps of reeds.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"दृष्टीविषैः सप्तशीर्षैर्गुप्तं भोगिभिरद्भुतैः ।\nरक्षोभिश्च पिशाचैश्च रौद्रैर्भूतगणैस्तथा ।\nराक्षसीभिश्च संपूर्णमनेकैश्च मृगद्विजैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"It was guarded by wondrous serpents with seven heads and poisonous glances, and was filled with rakshasas, pishachas, fierce hosts of spirits, many rakshasis, and many beasts and birds.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"सा तत्र सहसा गत्वा शैलपृष्ठं सुदुर्गमम् ।\nप्राक्षिपत्काञ्चने कुण्डे शुक्रं सा त्वरिता सती ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"She went suddenly to that very hard-to-reach mountain top and quickly threw the seed into a golden pool.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"शिष्टानामपि सा देवी सप्तर्षीणां महात्मनाम् ।\nपत्नीसरूपतां कृत्वा कामयामास पावकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then the goddess took the forms of the other wives of the great sages, one after another, and made love to Agni.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"दिव्यरूपमरुन्धत्याः कर्तुं न शकितं तया ।\nतस्यास्तपःप्रभावेण भर्तृशुश्रूषणेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"But she could not take Arundhati's divine form, because of Arundhati's austere power and her service to her husband.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"षट्कृत्वस्तत्तु निक्षिप्तमग्ने रेतः कुरूत्तम ।\nतस्मिन्कुण्डे प्रतिपदि कामिन्या स्वाहया तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Best of the Kurus, that seed was cast six times into the pool by loving Svaha on the first lunar day.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"तत्स्कन्नं तेजसा तत्र संभृतं जनयत्सुतम् ।\nऋषिभिः पूजितं स्कन्नमनयत्स्कन्दतां ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The seed that fell and was gathered there with fierce energy produced a son. Honored by the sages, the one who fell (skanna) came to be called Skanda.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"षट्शिरा द्विगुणश्रोत्रो द्वादशाक्षिभुजक्रमः ।\nएकग्रीवस्त्वेककायः कुमारः समपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Kumara came into being with six heads, double ears, twelve eyes and arms in order, one neck and one body.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"द्वितीयायामभिव्यक्तस्तृतीयायां शिशुर्बभौ ।\nअङ्गप्रत्यङ्गसंभूतश्चतुर्थ्यामभवद्गुहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He became manifest on the second day, appeared as a child on the third, and on the fourth Guha had his limbs and parts complete.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"लोहिताभ्रेण महता संवृतः सह विद्युता ।\nलोहिताभ्रे सुमहति भाति सूर्य इवोदितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surrounded by a great red cloud with lightning, he shone like the rising sun in a vast red cloud.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"गृहीतं तु धनुस्तेन विपुलं लोमहर्षणम् ।\nन्यस्तं यत्त्रिपुरघ्नेन सुरारिविनिकृन्तनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He took up a huge, hair-raising bow that the destroyer of Tripura had laid aside, which cuts down the gods' enemies.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"तद्गृहीत्वा धनुःश्रेष्ठं ननाद बलवांस्तदा ।\nसंमोहयन्निवेमान्स त्रीँल्लोकान्सचराचरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Taking up that best of bows, the mighty one roared, as if bewildering these three worlds with their moving and unmoving beings.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"तस्य तं निनदं श्रुत्वा महामेघौघनिस्वनम् ।\nउत्पेततुर्महानागौ चित्रश्चैरावतश्च ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Hearing his roar, like the thunder of great rain clouds, two great elephants, Chitra and Airavata, leapt up.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"तावापतन्तौ संप्रेक्ष्य स बालार्कसमद्युतिः ।\nद्वाभ्यां गृहीत्वा पाणिभ्यां शक्तिं चान्येन पाणिना ।\nअपरेणाग्निदायादस्ताम्रचूडं भुजेन सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Seeing them rush at him, he, bright as the young sun, took a spear in two hands, and with another hand took a red-crested cock, the son of Agni, in an arm.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"महाकायमुपश्लिष्टं कुक्कुटं बलिनां वरम् ।\nगृहीत्वा व्यनदद्भीमं चिक्रीड च महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He took the huge cock clinging to him, best of the strong, made a terrible cry and played with it, mighty one.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"द्वाभ्यां भुजाभ्यां बलवान्गृहीत्वा शङ्खमुत्तमम् ।\nप्राध्मापयत भूतानां त्रासनं बलिनामपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The strong one took a superb conch in two arms and blew it, a sound that frightens even the strong.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"द्वाभ्यां भुजाभ्यामाकाशं बहुशो निजघान सः ।\nक्रीडन्भाति महासेनस्त्रीँल्लोकान्वदनैः पिबन् ।\nपर्वताग्रेऽप्रमेयात्मा रश्मिमानुदये यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"With two arms he struck the sky many times. Playing, Mahasena shone, drinking in the three worlds with his faces, immeasurable in spirit on the mountain top, like the radiant sun at dawn.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"स तस्य पर्वतस्याग्रे निषण्णोऽद्भुतविक्रमः ।\nव्यलोकयदमेयात्मा मुखैर्नानाविधैर्दिशः ।\nस पश्यन्विविधान्भावांश्चकार निनदं पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Seated on top of that mountain, of wondrous valor and immeasurable spirit, he looked about the directions with his many faces. Seeing various sights, he roared again.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"तस्य तं निनदं श्रुत्वा न्यपतन्बहुधा जनाः ।\nभीताश्चोद्विग्नमनसस्तमेव शरणं ययुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Hearing his roar, people fell down in many places; frightened and troubled, they took refuge in him.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"ये तु तं संश्रिता देवं नानावर्णास्तदा जनाः ।\nतानप्याहुः पारिषदान्ब्राह्मणाः सुमहाबलान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The people of various colors who took refuge in that god, brahmins say, are his very powerful attendants.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"स तूत्थाय महाबाहुरुपसान्त्व्य च ताञ्जनान् ।\nधनुर्विकृष्य व्यसृजद्बाणाञ्श्वेते महागिरौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The mighty-armed one rose, comforted those people, drew his bow and shot arrows at the great white mountain.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"बिभेद स शरैः शैलं क्रौञ्चं हिमवतः सुतम् ।\nतेन हंसाश्च गृध्राश्च मेरुं गच्छन्ति पर्वतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"With his arrows he split the mountain Krauncha, Himalaya's son, and through it swans and vultures go to Mount Meru.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"स विशीर्णोऽपतच्छैलो भृशमार्तस्वरान्रुवन् ।\nतस्मिन्निपतिते त्वन्ये नेदुः शैला भृशं भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"That mountain fell shattered, crying out in great distress. When it fell, other mountains shrieked in fear.\""}},{"n":33,"text":"स तं नादं भृशार्तानां श्रुत्वापि बलिनां वरः ।\nन प्राव्यथदमेयात्मा शक्तिमुद्यम्य चानदत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Though he heard that cry of the afflicted, the best of the strong, immeasurable in spirit, was not troubled; he raised his spear and roared.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"सा तदा विपुला शक्तिः क्षिप्ता तेन महात्मना ।\nबिभेद शिखरं घोरं श्वेतस्य तरसा गिरेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then the great spear cast by that great being split the terrible peak of the white mountain with force.\""}},{"n":35,"text":"स तेनाभिहतो दीनो गिरिः श्वेतोऽचलैः सह ।\nउत्पपात महीं त्यक्त्वा भीतस्तस्मान्महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Struck by it, the white mountain, in misery, left the earth with the other mountains and rose up, in fear of that great one.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"ततः प्रव्यथिता भूमिर्व्यशीर्यत समन्ततः ।\nआर्ता स्कन्दं समासाद्य पुनर्बलवती बभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then the earth, in pain, broke apart on every side. Going to Skanda in distress, she became strong again.\""}},{"n":37,"text":"पर्वताश्च नमस्कृत्य तमेव पृथिवीं गताः ।\nअथायमभजल्लोकः स्कन्दं शुक्लस्य पञ्चमीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The mountains bowed to him and went back to the earth. And so this world worships Skanda on the fifth day of the bright fortnight.\""}}]}]}